Subject: [PATCH] arm/vvc: enable Clang NEON vectorization for 8-bit ALF gradients

ARMv7 companion to the ALF classification work tracked in:
https://code.ffmpeg.org/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/pulls/24925
ARM64 upstream snapshot: https://patchwork.ffmpeg.org/project/ffmpeg/patch/61096/
Applies after 0010 on FFmpeg master e0e6ca1e29ef3f6b1e9b7d8656fe341eee8cf647.

Clang's Cortex-A8 cost model leaves the 8-bit gradient loop scalar, while
10/12-bit gradients and directional sums already use compiler-generated NEON.
Request vectorization only for 8-bit ARM with NEON enabled, preserving the
existing classifier, alias checks, scalar tails and 64-bit index decisions.
The complete classifier measured 1.50-1.70x faster on the tested ARMv7 Xiaomi
with NDK29/API24/O3; a separate manual sum backend measured 1-3% slower and
is deliberately omitted. This is a local measured ARMv7 adaptation.

diff --git a/libavcodec/vvc/filter_template.c b/libavcodec/vvc/filter_template.c
index 80d1ac9..1b26dfa 100644
--- a/libavcodec/vvc/filter_template.c
+++ b/libavcodec/vvc/filter_template.c
@@ -313,6 +313,9 @@ void FUNC2(ff_vvc_alf_classify, BIT_DEPTH, _c)(int *class_idx, int *transpose_id
         else if (y == vb_pos + ALF_GRADIENT_BORDER)
             s0 = s1;
 
+#if defined(__clang__) && ARCH_ARM && HAVE_NEON && BIT_DEPTH == 8
+#pragma clang loop vectorize(enable)
+#endif
         for (int x = 0; x < w; x += ALF_GRADIENT_STEP) {
             //two points a time
             const pixel *a0  = s0 + x;
